                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1a2e22b0-c294-3d67-8bce-44a6b29a29e2",
                        "entry_id": "6e0ee425-9425-3262-8d99-8544cb959ba4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "матем., физ. составная часть сложного объекта"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fdcd9cad-48af-4011-9868-6ab2a4c3018d",
                                "sense_id": "1a2e22b0-c294-3d67-8bce-44a6b29a29e2",
                                "text": "Компонента вектора."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "410f4651-f25f-4b9e-9ace-4495f391cc66",
                                "sense_id": "1a2e22b0-c294-3d67-8bce-44a6b29a29e2",
                                "text": "Последняя компонента дисперсии затем используется для анализа статистической значимости различия между средними значениями."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6abb2057-a7fe-43d5-aac5-0c96e5cfc53a",
                        "source_entry_id": "6e0ee425-9425-3262-8d99-8544cb959ba4",
                        "source_sense_id": "1a2e22b0-c294-3d67-8bce-44a6b29a29e2",
                        "target_lang_word": "multiplier",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "multiplier",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "96fe5914-ab72-3bc0-ba0f-556b7b085398",
                                        "entry_id": "95fdf28b-8892-38cc-8f78-936fc38c533b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A number by which another (the multiplicand) is to be multiplied."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c1aec9d-fb70-4c9c-9341-d82fc09404e9",
                                                "sense_id": "96fe5914-ab72-3bc0-ba0f-556b7b085398",
                                                "text": "In the expression 5 × 7, the \"5\" is a multiplier."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a386106-e038-4a85-97c1-9bf94be7e35c",
                                                "sense_id": "96fe5914-ab72-3bc0-ba0f-556b7b085398",
                                                "text": "The score multiplier increases each time you complete a level of the video game."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78448a8e-5388-408c-811c-a584d9cc9187",
                                                "sense_id": "96fe5914-ab72-3bc0-ba0f-556b7b085398",
                                                "text": "The electron number constraint unlike the idempotency constraint can be represented by a single equation. For this reason, one can properly incorporate this constraint using a Lagrange multiplier and defining an effective chemical potential"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e166682c-6c30-49c6-bfe6-1e1a96b5f0d8",
                                                "sense_id": "96fe5914-ab72-3bc0-ba0f-556b7b085398",
                                                "text": "After studying a recursive formulation and the associated Bellman equation, in section 5.5 we analyze a Lagrangian formulation that provides useful insights about how Lagrange multipliers on transition laws relate to gradients of value functions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "050f4a91-ef09-4c39-b79d-c9dbc7791e00",
                                                "sense_id": "96fe5914-ab72-3bc0-ba0f-556b7b085398",
                                                "text": "But that can be ignored, because the USTR has set ε at 4 and φ at 0.25, so when computed give an overall multiplier of 1 for the imports number. And multiplying by 1 makes no difference at all."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5fcd1557-5e88-3183-b899-9eb638821282",
                                        "entry_id": "95fdf28b-8892-38cc-8f78-936fc38c533b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An adjective indicating the number of times something is to be multiplied."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5e4fb6e-bfd3-4613-81ad-26c3502d7c3e",
                                                "sense_id": "5fcd1557-5e88-3183-b899-9eb638821282",
                                                "text": "English multipliers include \"double\" and \"triple\"."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb168018-0ae7-30b0-91a8-38776faa5e45",
                                        "entry_id": "95fdf28b-8892-38cc-8f78-936fc38c533b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ratio used to estimate total economic effect for a variety of economic activities."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b05ed9c6-6f7b-4cc4-9989-7692bfdb24cc",
                                                "sense_id": "cb168018-0ae7-30b0-91a8-38776faa5e45",
                                                "text": "There is a second-round effect of crowding in higher private investment as public sector contractors tool up to meet the public contracts, and then a third – as all firms adjust to the higher level of demand by raising business investment levels – of more crowding in and so-called “multiplier effects”."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1341f7e0-1787-3798-8d2f-f22479a47939",
                                        "entry_id": "95fdf28b-8892-38cc-8f78-936fc38c533b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several devices used to enhance a signal"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e46da3a-47fc-3c2a-a742-412882d650c9",
                                        "entry_id": "95fdf28b-8892-38cc-8f78-936fc38c533b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several devices used to enhance a signal",
                                            "a coil; when Johann Schweigger in 1820 invented the electric coil, increasing the electro-magnetic field from a single wire, this invention was called a multiplier."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fff0f4b3-84a6-313a-9b52-ad8499e97207",
                                        "entry_id": "95fdf28b-8892-38cc-8f78-936fc38c533b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A multiplier onion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbba24b4-05d7-4a6d-bbcd-05d0e1162d3d",
                                                "sense_id": "fff0f4b3-84a6-313a-9b52-ad8499e97207",
                                                "text": "Shallots are the most prolific of all the multipliers, and easier to grow than onions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ad1d9834-74ed-4b52-b025-a6d9a02b1fa4",
                        "source_entry_id": "6e0ee425-9425-3262-8d99-8544cb959ba4",
                        "source_sense_id": "1a2e22b0-c294-3d67-8bce-44a6b29a29e2",
                        "target_lang_word": "component",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "component",
